  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\epsilon_0$ denotes the permittivity of free space and $\\Phi_{\\mathrm{E}}$ is the flux of the electric field through the area bounded by the closed surface, then dimension of $\\left(\\epsilon_0 \\frac{\\mathrm{~d} \\phi_{\\mathrm{E}}}{\\mathrm{dt}}\\right)$ are that of :",
